Caskey Fonts — license scope

This is a multi-license repository, not a blanket relicensing of upstream fonts.

* Caskey Mono, its historical Rob Mono Hinted font snapshots, and the included
  DejaVu Sans Mono source fonts retain their upstream Bitstream Vera / applicable
  Arev terms. See LICENSES/Bitstream-Vera-and-Arev.txt and the license beside the
  released fonts. DejaVu's own changes are public domain. Our independently
  copyrightable additions are offered under MIT-0, with no extra restrictions;
  the upstream conditions still govern the combined font files.
* Caskey Narrow, its historical Iosevka-derived font snapshots, and its derivative
  build plan are licensed under SIL OFL 1.1: LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt. No new Reserved
  Font Names are declared. The existing upstream copyright notice is preserved.
* Independently written Python/C tools and original project documentation are
  MIT-0: LICENSES/MIT-0.txt. Copied upstream license/attribution text retains its
  upstream terms. Tool licensing does not override font licensing.

Both upstream font licenses permit free use, modification, embedding and
redistribution, including commercial use, subject to their terms. They restrict
selling the fonts by themselves. OFL derivatives must stay under OFL. We cannot
remove these upstream conditions or offer the entire fonts as MIT/public domain.
No Caskey-specific attribution requirement or font-name reservation is added
beyond the requirements of the applicable upstream licenses.

The authoritative texts accompany each family in fonts/*/LICENSE.txt and are
embedded in font name-table license records. ATTRIBUTION.md records provenance.
